<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to make provision for granting leave to
judges to enable them to accept and hold office in certain judicial offices in
the service of the Independent State of Papua New
Guinea.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8220318e-6d65-4d8e-8345-7daa7720fc57"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_630da607-594c-455b-9534-659e79de4c49"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act may be cited as the <legref
refid="act-1979-177" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Judicial Office (Papua New Guinea) Act
1979</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a0cfaf63-423d-496a-8b3d-0c2ea994afe4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_b041f361-f83f-4065-8958-073b5d297c3f"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Interpretation</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4809dc84-8958-443e-8c4c-3edb35d6bf20"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_11cb91a3-9367-46ca-935b-a41da31488b9"
id="sec.2-def.appointedday"><b><i>appointed day</i></b></defterm> means a day
specified in a proclamation under subsection (2) as the appointed day for the
purposes of this Act.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_eda9819e-d8f0-4d63-9791-542eb50eb33b"
id="sec.2-def.headofthejurisdiction"><b><i>head of the
jurisdiction</i></b></defterm>:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_118cd9c3-0c0e-41e6-a4ca-7ff40734644e" id="sec.2-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in relation to a judge of the Supreme Court of
New South Wales, means the Chief Justice of that Court,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e8643428-6616-41e2-a39e-a1616c8ec839" id="sec.2-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in relation to a member of the Industrial
Commission of New South Wales, means the President of that
Commission,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2c6df316-b488-4493-85f3-cc5bf465ab2c" id="sec.2-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in relation to a judge of the District Court,
means the Chief Judge of that Court, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e0382779-8b0d-48ed-8a1e-9d4e6825453a" id="sec.2-ssec.1-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in relation to a member of the Workers&#8217;
Compensation Commission, means the Chairman of that
Commission.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_adea723a-16c5-476d-a157-01933e2af760"
id="sec.2-def.judge"><b><i>judge</i></b></defterm> has the meaning ascribed
thereto by section 2 (1) of the <legref refid="act-1953-041" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Judges&#8217; Pensions Act
1953</i></name></legref>, but does not include a person in his capacity as
Chairman of the Crown Employees Appeal Board.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0114b9e4-aa6d-4458-a86c-a24bbb5d1e58"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, by proclamation published in
the Gazette, specify a day as the appointed day for the purposes of this
Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5fdd8aa1-3ea2-4b5a-8ee4-5ce7ffdcf1de"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_4efb355e-4be2-43da-b818-38aafa89000d"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Leave to take judicial office in the Independent State of
Papua New Guinea</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d90a743f-9011-49c9-b6d9-aa65d1e19119"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor, on application made by a judge,
may, by instrument in writing, with the concurrence in writing of the
appropriate head of the jurisdiction, grant to that judge leave for him to be
absent from his office as a judge for the purpose of enabling him to accept
and hold the judicial office in the service of the Independent State of Papua
New Guinea that is specified in the instrument.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_de6ce2b4-00eb-41a6-a87f-c85badf4581a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Leave granted to a judge under subsection (1)
commences on the day specified in the instrument granting him the leave as the
day on which the leave commences and expires:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a9ee02de-3b64-4d7f-885c-d088d0a65806" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">upon the expiration of the period (being a period
not exceeding 12 months) specified in that instrument as the period for which
it was granted or of such additional period or periods as the Governor, on
application made by the judge, may, by instrument in writing,
determine,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_bbda7461-2589-42e2-88f5-fcb260efa70d" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">upon the expiration of the period specified in
the instrument granting him the leave as the period within which he is to take
office in the judicial office so specified, unless he has taken office in that
judicial office before the expiration of that period,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_08aa25b5-71c5-40a5-b7b5-1aef9a0e2334" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">upon his ceasing, otherwise than by reason of his
death, to hold the judicial office specified in the instrument granting him
the leave,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6a61bafc-9602-4a89-b873-e7d88fb55ab8" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">upon his attaining the retiring age for judges
holding the office of judge, being the office of judge of the same kind as
that held by him immediately before the leave commenced, if he attains that
age before his leave would, but for this paragraph, expire,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4a029e0f-3ef4-4e95-8a66-a8d3668398f3" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">upon his death, if he dies before his leave
would, but for this paragraph, expire,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">whichever first happens.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_32914bd6-1702-4968-9e0f-c3d48f2163b7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Leave shall not be granted to a judge under
subsection (1):</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3ecdaaff-be77-41c7-8fff-e213d3413a47" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to commence earlier than the appointed day,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_31df91d5-c685-4e78-8498-973452fa91ec" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to expire after the expiration of 2 years after
the appointed day.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4b5def24-dcf9-4fac-b20b-2c4f40ba4b01"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_d66148e9-f375-4c13-8cea-9b7941cad354"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Judge&#8217;s status while on leave</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">While a judge is on leave granted to him under
section 3 (1) he retains the office as a judge held by him immediately before
the leave commenced but is not entitled to exercise or perform any
jurisdiction, powers, authorities, duties or functions as the holder of that
office of judge.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_910b44ea-e0ae-4f5d-8a35-021e10cdc00e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_6107b07b-93ff-497d-9104-b47806071d08"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Resumption of office by judge</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Upon the expiration, under section 3 (2) (a), (b)
or (c), of leave granted to a judge under section 3 (1) the judge is entitled
to, and shall, resume the exercise and performance of the jurisdiction,
powers, authorities, duties and functions attaching to the office as a judge
held by him immediately before the leave commenced.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0d07c5c8-dac3-4718-9f0d-d4e40aa22e5e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_98a96fbc-ca86-4fba-a864-1d8a4d10ff92"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Operation of <legref refid="act-1953-041" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Judges&#8217; Pensions Act
1953</i></name></legref></b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The <legref refid="act-1953-041" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Judges&#8217; Pensions Act
1953</i></name></legref> applies to and in respect of a judge to whom leave
has been granted under section 3 (1) as if any period of that leave taken by
him were, for the purposes of that Act, part of the period of his service as a
judge.</txt></block></level>
</content>


